content.thinking:
OK so the comment says "DON'T add to scene — weapon will be attached to player socket". This is correct.

Now let me look at the problematic line in `animateViewModelWeapon`:
```javascript
this.scene.remove(source.mesh);
```

This removes `source.mesh` from the scene. But `source.mesh` was NEVER added to the scene in the first place! So this line does nothing (except potentially throw an error if `source.mesh` doesn't have a parent).

Actually, wait. Looking at the `Weapon` constructor more carefully, the mesh is created but NOT added to the scene (the `this.scene?.add(group)` line is commented out). So `source.mesh.parent` should be null, and `this.scene.remove(source.mesh)` should do nothing.

OK so this is not the issue.

Let me now focus on finding the actual problem. The user says the weapon disappears. From my testing:
1. The view weapon exists and is visible
2. All child meshes are visible
3. The positions are correct

But the user says it disappears. Let me now consider that maybe the problem is with the WEAPON MODEL ITSELF — maybe the model is being removed from the scene somewhere, or the geometry is being disposed.

Actually, let me re-read the `animateViewModelWeapon` method one more time:

```javascript
try {
    const source = new Weapon(weaponType, this.scene);
    // ...
    const viewClone = source.mesh.clone();
    // ...
    this.scene.remove(source.mesh);  // <-- This removes source.mesh from scene
    // ...
    this.fpArms.add(viewClone);
    // ...
}
```

The `source.mesh` is removed from the scene. But since `source.mesh` was never added to the scene in the first place, this line does nothing.


The `viewClone` gets added to `fpArms`, which is a child of the camera. I think the real problem might be that the third-person weapon is being hidden during initialization — looking at the constructor, `currentWeapon` is set to `this.fists` which doesn't render, so the knife never gets attached or shown in the first place. The view weapon exists and the third-person weapon is positioned correctly, but the player's camera starts facing away from it in third-person mode. Let me check the camera controller to confirm the initial orientation.

